{
"dur": 81.74,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 3.446,
"text": "Back at camp, it's afternoon, and the pace slows down.",
"end": 3.721
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 3.721,
"vo_start": 3.996,
"vo_end": 10.578,
"text": "People sit in the shade and talk. Kids play. Someone combs through a friend's hair while the conversation wanders.",
"end": 10.853
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 10.853,
"vo_start": 11.128,
"vo_end": 15.475,
"text": "Someone is drilling tiny holes through small shells, to string them as a necklace.",
"end": 15.75
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 15.75,
"vo_start": 16.025,
"vo_end": 22.458,
"text": "We know people did this, because at Blombos Cave in South Africa, archaeologists found shell beads about seventy-five thousand years old.",
"end": 22.733
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 22.733,
"vo_start": 23.008,
"vo_end": 31.327,
"text": "Dozens of tiny snail shells, each pierced and worn smooth where a string rubbed against it. Some were brought from river mouths kilometres away.",
"end": 31.602
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 31.602,
"vo_start": 31.877,
"vo_end": 36.915,
"text": "Gathered, carried home and drilled by hand. Not to eat. Just to look good.",
"end": 37.19
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 37.19,
"vo_start": 37.465,
"vo_end": 43.784,
"text": "And in 2008, in Hohle Fels cave in Germany, researchers pieced together a flute carved from a vulture's wing bone.",
"end": 44.059
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 44.059,
"vo_start": 44.334,
"vo_end": 47.972,
"text": "It's around forty thousand years old, and it has five finger holes.",
"end": 48.247
},
{
"i": 9,
"start": 48.247,
"vo_start": 48.522,
"vo_end": 53.522,
"text": "Someone in the Ice Age made an instrument. Someone else had the time to learn to play it.",
"end": 53.797
},
{
"i": 10,
"start": 53.797,
"vo_start": 54.072,
"vo_end": 59.912,
"text": "Now think about what kept you alive here. No money. No police. No hospital.",
"end": 60.187
},
{
"i": 11,
"start": 60.187,
"vo_start": 60.462,
"vo_end": 65.302,
"text": "If your hunt fails, or you break a leg and can't walk for a month, the only safety net is other people.",
"end": 65.577
},
{
"i": 12,
"start": 65.577,
"vo_start": 65.852,
"vo_end": 71.12,
"text": "If people like you, they feed you. If they don't, nobody owes you anything.",
"end": 71.395
},
{
"i": 13,
"start": 71.395,
"vo_start": 71.67,
"vo_end": 80.79,
"text": "So those slow afternoons of talking and joking weren't wasted. They were insurance. Friendships were your bank, your hospital and your pension, all at once.",
"end": 81.74
}
],
